    id: "cons-2015-ol-q2-b", topicId: "cons-6-2", conceptId: "external-wall-insulation-b",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2015 OL Q2(b)",
    stem: "The sketch shows a dwelling house which was built over 40 years ago. The external wall is a 300 mm concrete block wall with a 100 mm cavity. There is no insulation in the cavity. It is proposed to insulate the external wall by: filling the cavity with insulation and adding an external system of insulation to the wall.",
    questionText: "Discuss two advantages of insulating the external walls of the house.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "advantages", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Two advantages of insulating the external walls of the house", marks: 10, contextNote: "Two distinct advantages, 5 marks each, discussed rather than just named. Such as: reduced heat loss and a warmer house; improved thermal comfort with no extremes of heat or cold; lower energy bills; less fossil fuel burned to heat the house, which is better for the environment; improved U-value and Building Energy Rating (BER); reduced condensation and mould; the wall retains heat and acts as a heat store. Do not credit the same advantage twice.", permittedMarks: [0,5,10] },
    ],
