    id: "cons-2023-ol-q3-complete", topicId: "cons-5-2", conceptId: "solar-hot-water-complete",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2023 OL Q3 — complete",
    stem: "The sketch shows a dwelling house which has a solar collector on the roof. The solar collector provides hot water for the household.",
    questionText: "(a) Draw a large freehand sketch of the given house. On your sketch, show the pipework necessary to connect the solar collector to the hot water cylinder and supply hot water to a shower. Include the following in your sketch: flow and return pipes; expansion vessel; pipework to shower; all necessary valves. (b) Discuss two considerations when deciding the location of solar panels on a house.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 50,
    rows: [
    { id: "a-details", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Any 8 x 5 marks", marks: 40, contextNote: "Credit the best EIGHT acceptable items at 5 marks each, capped at 40. Marked items: solar collector; cold feed to collector; hot return to cylinder; cylinder; circulation pump; solar expansion vessel; storage tank; cold feed to cylinder; expansion pipe; hot water to shower and shower unit; valves. Typical sizes: Ø22 mm feed and return, a 250 l cylinder, a 24 l solar expansion vessel, a Ø28 mm expansion pipe, Ø22 mm hot water to the shower.", permittedMarks: [0,5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40] },
    { id: "b-consideration-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Consideration 1", marks: 5, contextNote: "Such as: the orientation of the roof; the position and proximity of neighbouring buildings; the pitch of the roof.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4,5] },
    { id: "b-consideration-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Consideration 2", marks: 5, contextNote: "A second, different consideration. Such as: whether the roof can support and secure the panels; the usable roof area; shading from trees; ease of maintenance and cleaning.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4,5] },
    ],
